      "reasoning": "Each answer is mathematically correct and supported by its own captured solution. q-161550: the shaded epigraph has boundary 2y=x²; the image frame does not create additional boundaries. q-161599: the region y≤−x²/2 has boundary −2y=x². q-161731: interior points lie strictly above y=0 and below y=2x/3, with 0<x<3. q-71888: the interior is the open upper half-disk x²+y²<4, y>0. The source's additional conditions x²+y²>0 and y<2 are redundant but correct, so option 2 gives an equivalent description. q-42157: R2←R2+4R1 gives the echelon matrix with rows [1,−6,2] and [0,0,−2]. The second row asserts 0=−2, so there is no solution, consistent with the earlier answer and this question's captured solution.",
